concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-2-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2(4) After section 4"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-2-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) A State or Territory judge or magistrate performing a conferred function, or exercising a conferred power, has the same protection and immunity as if he or she were performing that function, or exercising that power, as, or as a member of, a court (being the court of which the judge or magistrate is a member)." ;
    skos:definition "(4) A State or Territory judge or magistrate performing a conferred function, or exercising a conferred power, has the same protection and immunity as if he or she were performing that function, or exercising that power, as, or as a member of, a court (being the court of which the judge or magistrate is a member)."@en ;
