concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-2-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2(5) After section 4"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-2-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A person referred to in paragraph (1)(c) performing a conferred function, or exercising a conferred power, has the same protection and immunity as he or she would have in performing functions and powers as part of the person’s employment with a State or Territory court, as the case may be. This section applies regardless of when Commonwealth law made" ;
    skos:definition "(5) A person referred to in paragraph (1)(c) performing a conferred function, or exercising a conferred power, has the same protection and immunity as he or she would have in performing functions and powers as part of the person’s employment with a State or Territory court, as the case may be. This section applies regardless of when Commonwealth law made"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "46628e7386a030d03ec60b35bc95fb7c7dc5ea5853c0bafed2bf5430b139b7d9" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-2 ;
