concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "36 At the end of section 23WA"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-36 ;
    values:originalText "Add: Destroy forensic material or information (5) For the purposes of this Part, a person destroys forensic material taken from another person by a forensic procedure, the results of the analysis of the material or other information gained from it if the person destroys any means of identifying the forensic material or information with the person from whom it was taken or to whom it relates. Transgender persons (6) In this Part, a reference to a person being transgender or a transgender person is a reference to a person, whether or not the person is a recognised transgender person: (a) who identifies as a member of the opposite sex by living, or seeking to live, as a member of the opposite sex; or (b) who has identified as a member of the opposite sex by living as a member of the opposite sex; or (c) who, being of indeterminate sex, identifies as a member of a particular sex by living as a member of that sex; and includes a reference to the person being thought of as a transgender person, whether the person is, or was, in fact a transgender person. (7) In this Part (other than subsection (6)), a reference: (a) to a member of the opposite sex of a person means, if the person is a transgender person, a member of the opposite sex to the sex with which the transgender person identifies; and (b) to a member of the same sex as a person means, if the person is a transgender person, a member of the same sex as the sex with which the transgender person identifies.  Section 3" ;
    skos:definition "Add: Destroy forensic material or information (5) For the purposes of this Part, a person destroys forensic material taken from another person by a forensic procedure, the results of the analysis of the material or other information gained from it if the person destroys any means of identifying the forensic material or information with the person from whom it was taken or to whom it relates. Transgender persons (6) In this Part, a reference to a person being transgender or a transgender person is a reference to a person, whether or not the person is a recognised transgender person: (a) who identifies as a member of the opposite sex by living, or seeking to live, as a member of the opposite sex; or (b) who has identified as a member of the opposite sex by living as a member of the opposite sex; or (c) who, being of indeterminate sex, identifies as a member of a particular sex by living as a member of that sex; and includes a reference to the person being thought of as a transgender person, whether the person is, or was, in fact a transgender person. (7) In this Part (other than subsection (6)), a reference: (a) to a member of the opposite sex of a person means, if the person is a transgender person, a member of the opposite sex to the sex with which the transgender person identifies; and (b) to a member of the same sex as a person means, if the person is a transgender person, a member of the same sex as the sex with which the transgender person identifies.  Section 3"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "487f0f3e5f3047f586b5bfd51a057b79fcd98fdb223fcc399e685706691b53eb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-ss-7 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.15" .
