    values:originalText "(6) In this Part, a reference to a person being transgender or a transgender person is a reference to a person, whether or not the person is a recognised transgender person: (a) who identifies as a member of the opposite sex by living, or seeking to live, as a member of the opposite sex; or (b) who has identified as a member of the opposite sex by living as a member of the opposite sex; or (c) who, being of indeterminate sex, identifies as a member of a particular sex by living as a member of that sex; and includes a reference to the person being thought of as a transgender person, whether the person is, or was, in fact a transgender person." ;
    skos:definition "(6) In this Part, a reference to a person being transgender or a transgender person is a reference to a person, whether or not the person is a recognised transgender person: (a) who identifies as a member of the opposite sex by living, or seeking to live, as a member of the opposite sex; or (b) who has identified as a member of the opposite sex by living as a member of the opposite sex; or (c) who, being of indeterminate sex, identifies as a member of a particular sex by living as a member of that sex; and includes a reference to the person being thought of as a transgender person, whether the person is, or was, in fact a transgender person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5e90975a5b568e5103dfadf4dd0d0aee057527e683fafbadd0da728e5f07aeb7" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36 ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
