concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-20-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20-2 ;
    values:originalText "23XWA  Preventing the carrying out of forensic procedure A person is guilty of an offence if the person obstructs, hinders or resists a person carrying out a forensic procedure in accordance with this Part. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
