concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26(7) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) In determining whether to make an order under this section, a judge or magistrate is to take into account: (a) whether this Part would authorise the forensic procedure to be carried out in the absence of the order; and (b) the seriousness of the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence by the offender; and (c) whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure could assist law enforcement, whether Federal or otherwise; and  Carrying out of certain forensic procedures after conviction of serious and prescribed offenders  Division 6A Section 23XWP Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   27 (d) whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure is justified in all the circumstances." ;
    skos:definition "(7) In determining whether to make an order under this section, a judge or magistrate is to take into account: (a) whether this Part would authorise the forensic procedure to be carried out in the absence of the order; and (b) the seriousness of the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence by the offender; and (c) whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure could assist law enforcement, whether Federal or otherwise; and  Carrying out of certain forensic procedures after conviction of serious and prescribed offenders  Division 6A Section 23XWP Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   27 (d) whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure is justified in all the circumstances."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6087590ca1ad01f69963f213d837287a77d878fa4e97f6b49b5324d035587fa5" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Consider seriousness of circumstances and potential assistance to law enforcement when making an order." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf> ;
