doc:sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26(7) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) In determining whether to make an order under this section, a judge or magistrate is to take into account: (a) whether this Part would authorise the forensic procedure to be carried out in the absence of the order; and (b) the seriousness of the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence by the offender; and (c) whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure could assist law enforcement, whether Federal or otherwise; and  Carrying out of certain forensic procedures after conviction of serious and prescribed offenders  Division 6A Section 23XWP Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   27 (d) whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure is justified in all the circumstances." ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26(8) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) An order under this section takes effect immediately. However, the person who conducts any analysis of forensic material obtained as a result of carrying out the forensic procedure on an offender must not disclose the results of the analysis: (a) until the expiration of any appeal period or after the final determination of any appeal in relation to the offence concerned, whichever is the later; or (b) if the conviction is quashed. 23XWP  Carrying out forensic procedure following conviction" ;
    skos:definition "(8) An order under this section takes effect immediately. However, the person who conducts any analysis of forensic material obtained as a result of carrying out the forensic procedure on an offender must not disclose the results of the analysis: (a) until the expiration of any appeal period or after the final determination of any appeal in relation to the offence concerned, whichever is the later; or (b) if the conviction is quashed. 23XWP  Carrying out forensic procedure following conviction"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "77cd2c68098aff48654f7df2f4cc0aaf4d0e55f9df2fbc47748eae83bc88e218" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclose forensic analysis results until appeal period expires or conviction is quashed." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf, p.26" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-8-norm .
