concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26(3) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If a judge or magistrate orders an offender who is not in a prison or another place of detention to permit a forensic procedure to be carried out, the judge or magistrate may order the offender to attend at a police station (or other place specified by the judge or magistrate) within a period specified by the judge or magistrate to allow the forensic procedure to be carried out." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If a judge or magistrate orders an offender who is not in a prison or another place of detention to permit a forensic procedure to be carried out, the judge or magistrate may order the offender to attend at a police station (or other place specified by the judge or magistrate) within a period specified by the judge or magistrate to allow the forensic procedure to be carried out."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1df445703cb5bc10b8aaa94a6104872740c3fffb713e772a02019fbe418535ab" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Affidavit required for application under subsections (1) or (2) Order to permit forensic procedure" ;
    dc:description "affidavit" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
