concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26(4) Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26-2-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) An offender ordered to permit the carrying out of a forensic procedure is guilty of an offence if the offender, without reasonable excuse, refuses or fails to permit the forensic procedure to be carried out. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months. Note: A defendant bears the evidential burden in relation to the exception of reasonable excuse—see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(4) An offender ordered to permit the carrying out of a forensic procedure is guilty of an offence if the offender, without reasonable excuse, refuses or fails to permit the forensic procedure to be carried out. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months. Note: A defendant bears the evidential burden in relation to the exception of reasonable excuse—see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "35b7a61028b9c346aa5b74ff3f8ec53b4213b91b405c5b856906294d2ab8d605" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-26-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorized applicant may apply for order to take fingerprints of a child or incapable person. Refusal to permit forensic procedure without reasonable excuse is an offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf> ;
