concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-60 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "60 At the end of section 23YC"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-60 ;
    values:originalText "Add: (2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under section 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under section 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material obtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be retained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as practicable after the end of the period.  Carrying out of forensic procedures on volunteers and certain other persons  Division 6B Section 23XWV Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   35" ;
    skos:definition "Add: (2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under section 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under section 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material obtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be retained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as practicable after the end of the period.  Carrying out of forensic procedures on volunteers and certain other persons  Division 6B Section 23XWV Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   35"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1321e9f616ebc8cfb06c602d46a63731214e0e809c3fb22c5cd26fbc68ac7cc1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Forensic material must be destroyed after a specified period." ;
