concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-36-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "36 Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-36-2 ;
    values:originalText "Add: 23YDAA  Destruction of forensic material taken from offender after conviction quashed The constable who obtained an authority under section 23XWG, 23XWK or 23XWO for the carrying out of a forensic procedure on an offender whose conviction is quashed after the making of the order must ensure that any forensic material obtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure is destroyed as soon as practicable after the conviction is quashed. 23YDAB  Destruction of forensic material where related evidence is inadmissible If a magistrate finds that evidence described in subsection 23XX(3) relating to a forensic procedure is inadmissible under section 23XX, the Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, ensure that any forensic material taken from the person by that forensic procedure is destroyed." ;
    skos:definition "Add: 23YDAA  Destruction of forensic material taken from offender after conviction quashed The constable who obtained an authority under section 23XWG, 23XWK or 23XWO for the carrying out of a forensic procedure on an offender whose conviction is quashed after the making of the order must ensure that any forensic material obtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure is destroyed as soon as practicable after the conviction is quashed. 23YDAB  Destruction of forensic material where related evidence is inadmissible If a magistrate finds that evidence described in subsection 23XX(3) relating to a forensic procedure is inadmissible under section 23XX, the Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, ensure that any forensic material taken from the person by that forensic procedure is destroyed."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "05a33c35b373d2bf1328f03ac569539f10a15ddf56a399e90d551d079e6f4aee" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Ensure destruction of forensic material after conviction quashed." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf> ;
