concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-23yn a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23YN Retention of electronic recordings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-23yn ;
    values:originalText "(1) A tape recording made by a constable in accordance with this Part that is no longer required for investigative or evidentiary purposes may be retained for such other purposes, and for such period, as the Commissioner directs.  DNA database system  Division 8A Section 23YO Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   45 (2) A recording that is retained under this section is to be stored so as to protect it against unauthorised access or use by any person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A tape recording made by a constable in accordance with this Part that is no longer required for investigative or evidentiary purposes may be retained for such other purposes, and for such period, as the Commissioner directs.  DNA database system  Division 8A Section 23YO Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   45 (2) A recording that is retained under this section is to be stored so as to protect it against unauthorised access or use by any person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "67c50664c5ff4ea514063d30447e045dea7cef9ffa9ae5f3b1d5342d70ba0eb2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer ;
