    values:originalText "(2) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that was taken in accordance with a law of a State or a Territory may be retained or used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical purposes of the Commonwealth. The material or information may be retained or used even if its retention or use would, but for this subsection,  DNA database system  Division 8A Section 23YQ Crimes Amendment (Forensic Procedures) Act 2001                   47 constitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any provision of this Part relating to the carrying out of forensic procedures. Use and retention of forensic material taken before commencement of subsection" ;
    cof:pageNumber "46"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-1-sec-23yp-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23YP(3) Taking, retention and use of forensic material"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-23yp-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that is taken in accordance with a law of a State or a Territory, as in force immediately before the commencement of this subsection, may be retained or used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical purposes of the Commonwealth. The material or information may be retained or used even if its retention or use would, but for this subsection, constitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any provision of this Part relating to the carrying out of forensic procedures." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that is taken in accordance with a law of a State or a Territory, as in force immediately before the commencement of this subsection, may be retained or used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical purposes of the Commonwealth. The material or information may be retained or used even if its retention or use would, but for this subsection, constitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any provision of this Part relating to the carrying out of forensic procedures."@en ;
