concept:crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001-sch-2-sec-1-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 Subsection 3(1) (definition of foreign restraining order)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-1-2 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the definition, substitute: foreign restraining order means an order: (a) made under the law of a foreign country in respect of an offence against the law of that country; and (b) which is, or purports to be, made for the purpose of preserving property (whether or not the order also purports to do other things) including an order: (i) restraining a particular person or persons from dealing with the property; or (ii) freezing the property; or (iii) directing the seizure of the property; or (iv) directing that the property be taken into official custody or control." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the definition, substitute: foreign restraining order means an order: (a) made under the law of a foreign country in respect of an offence against the law of that country; and (b) which is, or purports to be, made for the purpose of preserving property (whether or not the order also purports to do other things) including an order: (i) restraining a particular person or persons from dealing with the property; or (ii) freezing the property; or (iii) directing the seizure of the property; or (iv) directing that the property be taken into official custody or control."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9597d9ead610712e505a8228ca7519ba9c378164731c266183b501be860df43f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "52"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definition of foreign restraining order" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-forensic-procedures-act-2001.pdf> ;
